 ## Overview
-This method is a display-only rendering technique for trained 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) scenes that projects 3D Gaussian distributions into 2D screen-space quads, sorts them by camera-space depth on the CPU, and renders them using hardware-instanced drawing with standard alpha blending [S1, S2, S5, S6, unofficial]. It solves the problem of visualizing large-scale, photorealistic 3D scenes reconstructed via Gaussian Splatting by treating each splat as a billboard-like primitive [S1, S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its siblings by relying on CPU-side depth sorting to resolve the non-commutative nature of alpha blending, avoiding the complexity of GPU-based tile-based rasterization or order-independent transparency (OIT) algorithms [S3, S6, unofficial]. Unlike [Tiled 2D Gaussian Splatting Rasterization](2061-tiled-2d-gaussian-splatting-rasterization.md), which rasterizes tiles, this method uses a single instanced draw call (or batched calls) to render all visible splats [S2, S5, unofficial].
+This method renders trained 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) scenes by projecting 3D Gaussians into 2D screen-space quads, sorting them by camera-space depth on the CPU, and drawing them using hardware-instanced rendering with standard alpha blending [S1, S2, S3, S5, S6, unofficial]. It solves the problem of visualizing large-scale, photorealistic 3D scenes on client-side hardware (Android, iOS, Web, ROS RViz) without requiring neural network inference or server-side ray tracing [S1, S3, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its siblings by performing the sorting explicitly on the CPU (often via radix sort or JS native sort) and using a single instanced draw call, whereas [Tiled 2D Gaussian Splatting Rasterization](2061-tiled-2d-gaussian-splatting-rasterization.md) performs sorting and rasterization entirely on the GPU, and [Gaussian Splat Rendering (Screen-Space Quad)](2075-gaussian-splat-rendering-screen-space-quad.md) describes the general mechanism without specifying the CPU-side sorting implementation [S2, S3, S6, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Inputs:** A set of $N$ 3D Gaussians defined by means $\mu$, covariances $\Sigma_{3D}$ (derived from rotations $q$ and scales $s$), opacities $\alpha$, and spherical harmonic (SH) coefficients $c$. A camera defined by view matrix $V$ and projection matrix $P$.
-*   **Outputs:** A 2D image buffer containing the composited RGB color and alpha channel.
+*   **Inputs:** A set of $N$ 3D Gaussians defined by means $\boldsymbol{\mu}$, covariances $\boldsymbol{\Sigma}_{3D}$ (derived from rotation $q$ and scale $s$), opacities $\alpha$, and spherical harmonic (SH) coefficients. Camera view matrix $\mathbf{V}$ and projection matrix $\mathbf{P}$.
+*   **Outputs:** A 2D image with color and alpha channels.
 
